---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy - LiveFonty" description="LiveFonty's privacy policy: the extension does not collect, store, or transmit any user data.">
  <main class="wrap">
    <article class="doc">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: July 25, 2026</p>

      <p>
        LiveFonty is a browser extension that lets you preview Google Fonts on the
        webpage you're currently viewing. This policy covers both the extension and
        the LiveFonty marketing website.
      </p>

      <h2>Chrome extension</h2>
      <p>
        The LiveFonty extension does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data,
        browsing history, or webpage content. It does not use analytics, tracking, or any
        third-party data services inside the extension.
      </p>

      <h2>Website analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The LiveFonty website (https://livefonty.de) uses Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID
        <code>G-2CWGCYDX28</code>) to measure traffic and key actions such as page views
        and download-button clicks. Analytics cookies are only set after you accept the
        cookie banner. You can reject analytics and still use the site. Google may process
        data according to
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How the extension works</h2>
      <p>
        When you select a font in the extension's popup, LiveFonty temporarily applies
        that font to the page you're currently viewing by loading the font's stylesheet
        directly from Google Fonts and adjusting that page's styling in your browser.
        This happens entirely on your device &mdash; nothing is sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        LiveFonty requests the <code>activeTab</code> and <code>scripting</code>
        permissions solely to apply your selected font to the tab you're actively
        viewing, only when you interact with the extension. It does not run in the
        background and cannot access any other tabs.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Font stylesheets and font files are loaded directly from Google Fonts
        (fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com). The website also loads Google
        Analytics when you accept cookies. Both are subject to
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:abdullahizzldin1@gmail.com">abdullahizzldin1@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to home</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <style>
    .doc {
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 56px 0 80px;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    }
    .updated {
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 300;
      margin: 0 0 32px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin: 32px 0 10px;
    }
    p {
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-weight: 300;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }
    code {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
      padding: 2px 6px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    a {
      color: var(--plum);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .back {
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
